Feature: File Operations
  Testing file creation and assertions

  Image: alpine:latest

  Scenario: Create and verify file
    Given a file "hello.txt" with content:
      Hello from smoko
    When I run "cat hello.txt"
    Then exit code is 0
    Then output contains "Hello from smoko"
    Then file "hello.txt" exists

  Scenario: Missing file check
    When I run "ls nonexistent.txt"
    Then exit code is not 0
    Then file "nonexistent.txt" does not exist

  Scenario: Create directory
    Given the directory "mydir" exists
    When I run "ls -d mydir"
    Then exit code is 0
    Then directory "mydir" exists
